From: m2391 device maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Restore opt-in StrictMode leak detection and penalties

DerpFest 17 enables activity and registration leak checks for all apps targeting
API 24+, even on user builds and with persist.sys.strictmode.disable=true.
It also unconditionally makes receiver/service-connection leaks fatal.

Restore AOSP defaults: keep file URI exposure protection, leave leak detection
to app/debug policies, and respect the selected penalty instead of forcing death.
QQ 9.3.80 loses its main process when QQScanActivity is destroyed; scan-to-web
also kills that process while QQBrowserActivity is opening in :tool.

This applies to frameworks/base, not to the device tree itself.

--- a/core/java/android/os/StrictMode.java
+++ b/core/java/android/os/StrictMode.java
@@ -1633,8 +1633,6 @@
         if (targetSdkVersion >= Build.VERSION_CODES.N) {
             builder.detectFileUriExposure();
             builder.penaltyDeathOnFileUriExposure();
-            builder.detectActivityLeaks();
-            builder.detectLeakedRegistrationObjects();
         }
 
         if (Build.IS_USER || DISABLE || SystemProperties.getBoolean(DISABLE_PROPERTY, false)) {
@@ -2768,9 +2766,7 @@
 
     /** @hide */
     public static void onVmPolicyViolation(Violation originStack) {
-        boolean forceDeath = originStack instanceof IntentReceiverLeakedViolation 
-            || originStack instanceof ServiceConnectionLeakedViolation;
-        onVmPolicyViolation(originStack, forceDeath);
+        onVmPolicyViolation(originStack, false);
     }
 
     /** @hide */
